WEBVTT

00:00:00.103 --> 00:00:06.786
PostgreSQL does not require a special PIVOT keyword
for the core patterns taught here You

00:00:06.799 --> 00:00:12.606
can use conditional aggregation One common form is
SUM with CASE

00:00:14.347 --> 00:00:21.467
PostgreSQL also supports FILTER on aggregate
functions which can be very readable Both

00:00:21.493 --> 00:00:27.414
approaches use the same underlying idea one grouped
output row with category-specific aggregate columns
